34,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The fixed costs are over 280,000 yen. More importantly, the fuel spending is incredibly lopsided; some of us pay far more than others.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,It seems auditing is a trap. I found that checking figures often leads to feelings of accusation and apologies.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My findings are frustrating. The car is often returned with the fuel light on and rubbish inside, and weekly trips keep collapsing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The diary confirms the usage is uneven, with weekends being far busier. Combined with the fuel data, the current split is illogical.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Recording every run took nearly an hour a week. Plus, those heavy-use weeks create total chaos in our schedules.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"If we keep a simple split, the heavy users are being subsidized. We need a system that reflects actual usage.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"But @Minako, if we track every kilometer to be ""fair,"" we risk the social friction I mentioned. We must be careful.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,Fairness doesn't matter if I can't rely on the car for my weekly needs. We need a way to guarantee access.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, logic must come first. We cannot ignore that some people are paying for others' trips. That is the real source of friction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I can't handle more recording. An hour a week just to track the car is too much mental effort.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We have a conflict between precision and peace. However, the financial gap is too large to ignore.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Other households said the worst parts are asking for favors constantly or people clinging to turns they don't need.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,That explains why the weekly trips collapse. Someone is likely holding the car without using it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,Which is why a diary or a fixed record is necessary. We need to stop the guesswork immediately.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,Is there any way to just... not have to negotiate every single time?,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I think we have enough information to consider our options. We need to balance cost, time, and reliability.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed. Let's look for the path of least resistance that still feels equitable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,As long as it ensures the car is clean and available when I need it.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"And as long as the payments are based on reality, not a guess.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just want the stress to stop.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
