60,3,1,talk,Minako,,"We have three options: Fixed Day Allocation, a Booking Calendar with distance-based costs, or a Primary Keeper.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option A seems the most harmonious. No one has to ask for favors; you just own your day.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A would solve my weekly trip problem. I would know exactly when the car is mine.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option B is the only one that is logically fair regarding fuel. Distance-based costs reflect actual usage.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option B sounds like more recording. @Shion, remember that the trial took an hour a week. I hate that.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Option C puts the burden on one person. It's simple, but is it fair to the keeper?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Option C still requires ""arranging use,"" which other households said sours the relationship. I dislike it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is clean. If I have Tuesday, I don't have to worry about who had it Monday or if it's there.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,But Option A ignores the fact that Saturdays are used three times more than Tuesdays. It's financially inefficient.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I don't care about the efficiency as much as the peace. Option A means no more negotiating.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Option A is a compromise. It's not perfectly precise, but it removes the auditing that @Benjamin fears.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Exactly. It replaces negotiation with a rule. It's the most elegant solution for the group's health.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I vote for Option A. It guarantees my schedule and reduces the handover chaos.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I still prefer B for the precision, but if the group finds the administration too taxing, A is a distant second.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm definitely for Option A. No more spreadsheets, no more arguing over hours.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,I will vote for Option A. It's a sustainable balance between equity and sanity.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Option A it is.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I'll concede to the majority, though I still find the cost distribution imperfect. Option A.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,Thank goodness. Option A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
